WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:12.516
Inside a box lay 25 tin soldiers.

2
00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:16.503
Each shouldered a rifle and wore a smart red uniform.

3
00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:25.103
When the lid was taken off the box, a little boy clapped his hands and cried with delight, "Soldiers, soldiers!"

4
00:00:25.104 --> 00:00:28.471
He lost no time setting them up on a table.

5
00:00:28.472 --> 00:00:34.740
All the soldiers were exactly alike except for one who had only one leg.

6
00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:39.725
But he stood just as well as the others—and just as proudly too.

7
00:00:39.726 --> 00:00:47.298
From where he stood, the tin soldier with one leg could see a delightful castle on a table near the window.

8
00:00:47.299 --> 00:00:50.508
In front of the castle stood a paper doll.

9
00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:57.342
She was a beautiful dancer and wore a dress of the palest pink, with a rose in her hair.

10
00:00:57.343 --> 00:01:02.630
"She would be the perfect wife for me!" thought the tin soldier.

11
00:01:02.631 --> 00:01:08.885
"But she lives in a palace and must be a princess, while I am only a soldier and live in a box.

12
00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:11.449
Nonetheless, I hope I get to meet her."

13
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:19.188
Late in the evening, the boy put the other soldiers back into their box, but to the tin soldier he said,

14
00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:25.407
"You must guard the others, brave soldier," and set him beside the box.

15
00:01:25.408 --> 00:01:31.263
After the boy left, all the other toys amused themselves with dances and games.

16
00:01:31.264 --> 00:01:36.790
The only ones who did not move were the tin soldier and the little dancer.

17
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:40.655
She stood on tiptoe, with her arms spread out.

18
00:01:40.656 --> 00:01:46.856
He, bravely on his one leg, did not take his eyes off her for a moment.

19
00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:54.280
When the clock struck twelve, up flew the lid of a Jack-in-the-box and out popped a goblin with a grin.

20
00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:58.303
"Tin soldier!" said the goblin, "Look away.

21
00:01:58.304 --> 00:02:01.161
You will never have the pretty dancer's heart."

22
00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:05.218
But the tin soldier ignored him and didn't say a word.

23
00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:10.487
"Ah! Tomorrow you will be punished," said the goblin.

24
00:02:10.488 --> 00:02:15.964
In the morning the boy and his friend decided to put the tin soldier by the window.

25
00:02:15.965 --> 00:02:28.499
Now, whether it was caused by the goblin or by a puff of wind, we do not know, but all at once the tin soldier fell headfirst into the garden below.

26
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.769
It was a terrific fall, and he landed under some flowers.

27
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:40.823
The little boy looked for him, and if the soldier had only called, "Here I am," the boy would easily have found him.

28
00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:47.344
But the soldier did not think it was proper to cry for help while he was in uniform.

29
00:02:47.345 --> 00:02:51.765
It began to rain, and the drops fell faster and harder.

30
00:02:51.766 --> 00:02:55.479
Two boys came along. "Look!" said one.

31
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.280
"It's a tin soldier! Let's send him for a sail."

32
00:02:59.281 --> 00:03:03.818
So they made a boat out of newspaper and stood the soldier in it.

33
00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:11.404
As he sailed away down the gutter, both boys ran alongside, clapping their hands.

34
00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:17.143
The waves were high and the current was strong, but the tin soldier showed no fear.

35
00:03:17.144 --> 00:03:22.354
Up ahead, the gutter flowed under an arch and into a long dark tunnel.

36
00:03:22.355 --> 00:03:28.835
"Where on earth am I going now!" thought the soldier as the boat carried him along.

37
00:03:28.836 --> 00:03:31.865
"Well, it is the fault of that goblin!

38
00:03:31.866 --> 00:03:37.023
Oh, if only the little dancer were with me in my boat, I wouldn't care about the dark!"

39
00:03:37.024 --> 00:03:40.936
At this moment, a big water rat swam up.

40
00:03:40.937 --> 00:03:46.068
"Do you have a pass?" asked the rat. "Show me your pass!"

41
00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:50.678
The tin soldier did not speak, but clung tightly to his gun.

42
00:03:50.679 --> 00:03:52.854
The boat rushed on.

43
00:03:52.855 --> 00:03:59.691
The rat showed its teeth and shouted, "Stop him, stop him; he doesn't have a pass!"

44
00:03:59.692 --> 00:04:05.370
But the current grew stronger, and the soldier's boat quickly left the rat behind.

45
00:04:05.371 --> 00:04:12.251
Up ahead, the tin soldier could see daylight, but he also heard the loud roar of water.

46
00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:18.097
Where the tunnel ended, the stream poured straight into a big canal.

47
00:04:18.098 --> 00:04:23.401
The boat rushed out of the tunnel and, in a gush of water, fell into the canal.

48
00:04:23.402 --> 00:04:30.185
Swirling around, the boat filled with water, but the tin soldier stood bravely at attention.

49
00:04:30.186 --> 00:04:35.305
As the waves rose over his head, he thought of the elegant little dancer.

50
00:04:35.306 --> 00:04:43.038
But much as he wished to see her again, he remembered that a soldier must bravely face his fate.

51
00:04:43.039 --> 00:04:47.093
Suddenly a great fish appeared and swallowed him up.

52
00:04:47.094 --> 00:04:51.682
It was dark inside that fish, worse than being in the tunnel!

53
00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:54.498
But the tin soldier showed no fear.

54
00:04:54.499 --> 00:05:01.372
The fish was caught, taken to the market, and sold to the same cook who lived in the boy's house.

55
00:05:01.373 --> 00:05:03.915
She cut the fish open with a knife.

56
00:05:03.916 --> 00:05:08.297
"Look, the tin soldier!" she called.

57
00:05:08.298 --> 00:05:15.045
Marveling at the soldier who had traveled so far and returned in a fish, she carried him to the boy.

58
00:05:15.046 --> 00:05:20.466
The goblin in the Jack-in-the-box was far from pleased to see the soldier return,

59
00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:26.468
but the happy boy set the soldier in his place on the table by the fire.

60
00:05:26.469 --> 00:05:34.234
To the soldier's delight, the dancer still stood in front of the castle, as pretty as he remembered her.

61
00:05:34.235 --> 00:05:38.073
She had tears in her eyes and a smile on her face.

62
00:05:38.074 --> 00:05:46.538
The soldier was so moved that he was ready to shed a tear of his own, but that would not have been proper for a soldier.

63
00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:50.764
The goblin, of course, was jealous when he saw their happiness.

64
00:05:50.765 --> 00:05:57.210
And whether the goblin knocked him, or the tin soldier fell, or some other tragedy occurred,

65
00:05:57.211 --> 00:06:04.240
it is impossible to say; but just then the tin soldier tumbled into the fireplace.

66
00:06:04.241 --> 00:06:10.889
The flames surrounded him with a horrible heat, and he felt that he was melting away.

67
00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:16.452
Whether it was from the heat of the fire or the grief in his heart, who can tell?

68
00:06:16.453 --> 00:06:26.287
A door was suddenly opened; a light wind caught the little dancer, and she fluttered like a fairy, straight into the fire to join the soldier.

69
00:06:26.288 --> 00:06:30.034
In a blaze, she was gone!

70
00:06:30.035 --> 00:06:34.140
The poor little soldier was reduced to a molten lump.

71
00:06:34.141 --> 00:06:43.118
But the next morning, when the maid cleaned away the ashes from the fireplace, she found a small, perfectly-shaped tin heart.

72
00:06:43.119 --> 00:06:49.274
And in its center was the rose from the dancer's hair.
